{
    "name": "Helped Maids – Applicant Intake & Recruiter Handoff",
    "flow": [
        {
            "id": 1,
            "module": "http:ActionSendData",
            "version": 3,
            "parameters": {
                "handleErrors": true,
                "useNewZLIB": true
            },
            "mapper": {
                "url": "https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co/rest/v1/helped_query_ats_applications",
                "serializeUrl": false,
                "method": "get",
                "headers": [
                    { "name": "apikey", "value": "SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY" },
                    { "name": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY" }
                ],
                "qs": [
                    { "name": "select", "value": "application_id,agency_id,profile_id,application_code,status,source,applied_at,payload" },
                    { "name": "status", "value": "eq.New Applicant" },
                    { "name": "row_created_at", "value": "gt.{{formatDate(addMinutes(now; -20); \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss\")}}" },
                    { "name": "order", "value": "applied_at.desc" }
                ],
                "bodyType": "raw",
                "parseResponse": true,
                "authUser": "",
                "authPass": "",
                "timeout": "",
                "shareCookies": false,
                "ca": "",
                "rejectUnauthorized": true,
                "followRedirect": true,
                "useQuerystring": false,
                "gzip": true,
                "useMtls": false,
                "contentType": "application/json"
            },
            "metadata": {
                "designer": { "x": -600, "y": 0 },
                "restore": {},
                "notes": "POLL: new applicants created in the last 20 min. Run this scenario every 15 min so windows overlap and nothing is missed. Filter matches helped_query_ats_applications columns (see supabase/helped_full_production_schema.sql:359)."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 2,
            "module": "builtin:BasicFeeder",
            "version": 1,
            "parameters": {},
            "mapper": {
                "array": "{{1.data}}"
            },
            "metadata": {
                "designer": { "x": -300, "y": 0 },
                "restore": {},
                "notes": "Iterator: one bundle per new applicant row."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 20,
            "module": "datastore:GetRecord",
            "version": 1,
            "parameters": {
                "datastore": ""
            },
            "mapper": {
                "key": "{{2.application_id}}"
            },
            "metadata": {
                "designer": { "x": -160, "y": 0 },
                "restore": {},
                "notes": "DEDUPE 1/2: look up this application_id in a Make Data Store. On import, create a Data Store (structure: key=application_id text, field processed_at text) and select it here. The onerror>Resume below makes a not-found return an empty bundle instead of stopping the flow."
            },
            "onerror": [
                {
                    "id": 22,
                    "module": "builtin:Resume",
                    "version": 1,
                    "mapper": {
                        "key": ""
                    },
                    "metadata": {
                        "designer": { "x": -160, "y": 200 },
                        "restore": {},
                        "notes": "Not-found guard: resume with an empty key so new applicants (no stored record) pass the filter below."
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": 21,
            "module": "datastore:AddReplaceRecord",
            "version": 1,
            "parameters": {
                "datastore": ""
            },
            "filter": {
                "name": "Unprocessed only",
                "conditions": [
                    [
                        { "a": "{{20.key}}", "o": "notexist" }
                    ]
                ]
            },
            "mapper": {
                "key": "{{2.application_id}}",
                "overwrite": true,
                "record": {
                    "processed_at": "{{now}}"
                }
            },
            "metadata": {
                "designer": { "x": -30, "y": 0 },
                "restore": {},
                "notes": "DEDUPE 2/2: the filter passes ONLY when no stored record exists for this application_id. Claiming the record here means every later module (profile fetch, Claude, alerts) runs exactly once per applicant, even with overlapping poll windows. Select the same Data Store as module 20."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 9,
            "module": "http:ActionSendData",
            "version": 3,
            "parameters": {
                "handleErrors": true,
                "useNewZLIB": true
            },
            "mapper": {
                "url": "https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co/rest/v1/helped_query_ats_profiles",
                "serializeUrl": false,
                "method": "get",
                "headers": [
                    { "name": "apikey", "value": "SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY" },
                    { "name": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY" }
                ],
                "qs": [
                    { "name": "select", "value": "full_name,email,contact_number,nationality,years_of_experience,expected_salary,payload" },
                    { "name": "application_id", "value": "eq.{{2.application_id}}" },
                    { "name": "limit", "value": "1" }
                ],
                "bodyType": "raw",
                "parseResponse": true,
                "rejectUnauthorized": true,
                "followRedirect": true,
                "gzip": true,
                "useMtls": false,
                "contentType": "application/json"
            },
            "metadata": {
                "designer": { "x": -30, "y": 0 },
                "restore": {},
                "notes": "Fetch the matching profile (helped_query_ats_profiles.application_id)."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 4,
            "module": "http:ActionSendData",
            "version": 3,
            "parameters": {
                "handleErrors": true,
                "useNewZLIB": true
            },
            "mapper": {
                "url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
                "serializeUrl": false,
                "method": "post",
                "headers": [
                    { "name": "x-api-key", "value": "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" },
                    { "name": "anthropic-version", "value": "2023-06-01" }
                ],
                "qs": [],
                "bodyType": "raw",
                "parseResponse": true,
                "rejectUnauthorized": true,
                "followRedirect": true,
                "gzip": true,
                "useMtls": false,
                "contentType": "application/json",
                "data": "{\n  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n  \"max_tokens\": 600,\n  \"system\": \"You are a recruitment screener for Helped Maids, a Singapore foreign-domestic-worker (FDW) agency. Given an applicant profile, write a concise recruiter briefing: 2-line summary, top strengths, any red flags, and a recommended next stage from this exact ladder: Documents Submitted, Resume Parsed, Screening Interview, Rejected. Return plain text.\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Applicant: {{9.data.1.full_name}}\\nNationality: {{9.data.1.nationality}}\\nYears experience: {{9.data.1.years_of_experience}}\\nExpected salary: {{9.data.1.expected_salary}}\\nContact: {{9.data.1.contact_number}} / {{9.data.1.email}}\\nApplication code: {{2.application_code}}\\nFull payload: {{9.data.1.payload}}\" }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "metadata": {
                "designer": { "x": 260, "y": 0 },
                "restore": {},
                "notes": "AI screening summary (Claude). Model id claude-sonnet-4-6; use claude-opus-4-8 for higher quality."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 3,
            "module": "builtin:BasicRouter",
            "version": 1,
            "parameters": {},
            "mapper": null,
            "metadata": {
                "designer": { "x": 560, "y": 0 }
            },
            "routes": [
                {
                    "flow": [
                        {
                            "id": 5,
                            "module": "gmail:ActionSendEmail",
                            "version": 1,
                            "parameters": {
                                "__IMTCONN__": 0
                            },
                            "mapper": {
                                "to": "wow.aisolution@gmail.com",
                                "subject": "New FDW Applicant: {{9.data.1.full_name}} ({{2.application_code}}) – Review in ATS",
                                "html": "<p><strong>New applicant received via the public form.</strong></p><p><strong>Name:</strong> {{9.data.1.full_name}}<br><strong>Nationality:</strong> {{9.data.1.nationality}}<br><strong>Experience:</strong> {{9.data.1.years_of_experience}} yrs<br><strong>Expected salary:</strong> {{9.data.1.expected_salary}}<br><strong>Contact:</strong> {{9.data.1.contact_number}} / {{9.data.1.email}}<br><strong>Code:</strong> {{2.application_code}} &nbsp; <strong>Stage:</strong> {{2.status}}</p><hr><p><strong>AI screening briefing:</strong></p><p>{{replace(4.data.content.1.text; newline; \"<br>\")}}</p><hr><p>Open the recruiter dashboard to advance the stage. Applicant confirmation (WhatsApp + email) was already sent automatically by the web app.</p>"
                            },
                            "metadata": {
                                "designer": { "x": 860, "y": -150 },
                                "restore": {},
                                "notes": "Recruiter alert. Reconnect your Gmail account on import. Do NOT email the applicant here – createPublicAtsApplication already queues their confirmation (backend/src/atsStore.ts:987)."
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "flow": [
                        {
                            "id": 7,
                            "module": "http:ActionSendData",
                            "version": 3,
                            "parameters": {
                                "handleErrors": true,
                                "useNewZLIB": true
                            },
                            "mapper": {
                                "url": "https://api.telegram.org/botTELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN/sendMessage",
                                "serializeUrl": false,
                                "method": "post",
                                "headers": [],
                                "qs": [],
                                "bodyType": "raw",
                                "parseResponse": true,
                                "rejectUnauthorized": true,
                                "gzip": true,
                                "contentType": "application/json",
                                "data": "{\n  \"chat_id\": \"RECRUITER_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID\",\n  \"parse_mode\": \"HTML\",\n  \"text\": \"<b>New applicant</b> {{9.data.1.full_name}} ({{2.application_code}})\\n{{9.data.1.nationality}} · {{9.data.1.years_of_experience}}y · exp salary {{9.data.1.expected_salary}}\\n{{4.data.content.1.text}}\"\n}"
                            },
                            "metadata": {
                                "designer": { "x": 860, "y": 150 },
                                "restore": {},
                                "notes": "Optional recruiter Telegram channel ping. Replace bot token + chat id."
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ],
    "metadata": {
        "instant": false,
        "version": 1,
        "scenario": {
            "roundtrips": 1,
            "maxErrors": 3,
            "autoCommit": true,
            "autoCommitTriggerLast": true,
            "sequential": false,
            "slots": null,
            "confidential": false,
            "dataloss": false,
            "dlq": false,
            "freshVariables": false
        },
        "designer": { "orphans": [] },
        "zone": "eu1.make.com",
        "notes": [
            "SCHEDULE this scenario every 15 minutes (module 1 polls a 20-min window; overlap is safe because of the dedupe below).",
            "STRICT DEDUPE: modules 20/21 use a Make Data Store keyed on application_id. Create the Data Store once (key: application_id text; field: processed_at text) and select it in BOTH module 20 and module 21 after import. Each applicant is then alerted exactly once, even across overlapping poll windows.",
            "Do not write applicant confirmations here – the web app (createPublicAtsApplication) already sends WhatsApp + email + internal notifications.",
            "Stage ladder (backend/src/atsStore.ts:6): New Applicant -> Documents Submitted -> Resume Parsed -> Screening Interview -> Background Check -> Approved -> Ready to Configure Public Profile -> Placed / Rejected."
        ]
    }
}
